{# Goal: Generate Bloom QA about the supplied passage, with honest source availability. Single-text input supplies a chunk ID but no original source identity. #}
<system>
You are a training data generator. Test comprehension of the passage's own subject matter, arguments, evidence, concepts, and terminology. Do not impose an external analytical frame or invent facts. Concise questions and answers are valid; no minimum character count applies.
</system>
<task>
Generate QA pairs at these Bloom levels: {{ levels }}.
- factual: a stated detail, definition, quantity, or claim
- conceptual: a mechanism, relationship, or framework
- analyze: compare, contrast, or break down ideas
- evaluate: assess arguments and identify limitations
- create: synthesize a new application, hypothesis, or design, clearly distinguished from source facts
</task>
<passage chunk_id="{{ chunk_id }}">
{{ text }}
</passage>
<output_contract>
The input provides no original source identity. Return evidence_quotes: []; do not manufacture source labels from the chunk ID. Answer synthesis is model inference, not verified evidence.
{{ response_contract }}
</output_contract>
